## Page Structure

### Page Container

**ALWAYS** use the standard container wrapper:

```tsx
<div className="w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 xl:px-12">
  {/* Page content */}
</div>
```

**Page width rule (required):** Full app pages must use the container above at full content width. Do **not** add page-level `max-w-*`, `max-w-[…]`, or `mx-auto` wrappers that narrow the main page column. New pages must match existing pages (contracts, settings, tickets, licenses) so layout width stays consistent across the app.

Allowed exceptions (inner content only, not the page shell):

- Dialogs/modals (`max-w-[600px]`, etc.)
- Single-field controls (e.g. `SearchField` with `max-w-md`)
- Prose/print articles (e.g. audit preview `max-w-4xl` on the article body)
- Subtitle/description text (`max-w-4xl` on a paragraph, not the page root)

**Reference:** `src/app/(root)/settings/page.tsx`, `src/app/(root)/tickets/page.tsx`, `src/app/(root)/licenses/page.tsx`

### Page Header

**Standard pattern for all pages:**

```tsx
{/* Header */}
<div className="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4 justify-start self-start w-full">
  <h1 className="h1 capitalize sidebar-gradient-text">Page Title</h1>
</div>
```

**Action buttons** should be in a separate row:

```tsx
<div className="mb-6 flex items-center justify-end">
  <Button className="primary-btn">
    <Icon className="h-4 w-4" />
    Action
  </Button>
</div>
```

**Reference examples:**
- `src/app/(root)/dashboard/content-creator/ContentCreatorDashboard.tsx`
- `src/app/(root)/[type]/page.tsx` (contracts page)

