## Dialog & Modal Standards

**Hard rule:** Do not deviate from the CAALM dialog template unless the user explicitly asks. Prefer corner **X** to dismiss; omit footer Cancel unless requested. Do not invent alternate dialog chrome (custom icon tiles, flat white headers, solid filled destructive CTAs instead of `.delete-btn`).

### Standard Dialog Structure

**ALL dialogs** must follow this structure:

```tsx
<Dialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={setIsOpen}>
  <DialogContent className="max-w-[600px] p-0 max-h-[90vh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 shadow-xl">
    {/* Professional Cap */}
    <div className="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 bg-[#d6d7d8] opacity-70 rounded-t-md" />

    {/* Header with gradient background */}
    <div className="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 py-4 border-b border-slate-200 mt-4">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-3 px-6">
        <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
          <IconComponent className="w-5 h-5 text-[#0f5384]" />
          <DialogTitle className="text-xl font-semibold sidebar-gradient-text">
            Dialog Title
          </DialogTitle>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p className="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 ml-14">
        Optional subtitle or description
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Scrollable Content */}
    <div className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-6 bg-slate-50">
      {/* Main content here */}
    </div>

    {/* Professional Footer — corner X dismisses; omit Cancel unless requested */}
    <div className="px-6 py-4 bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-end gap-3">
      <Button className="primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4">
        <Icon className="h-4 w-4" />
        Action
      </Button>
    </div>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

### Dialog Requirements

**ALWAYS:**
- Include professional cap bar at the top
- Use gradient header (`bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50`)
- Add `mt-4` to header div to account for cap bar
- Use `bg-slate-50` for scrollable content area
- Place icons directly next to title with `gap-3` and `text-[#0f5384]`
- Prefer corner X (`showCloseButton`) to dismiss; do not add footer Cancel unless the user asks
- Do not invent alternate dialog chrome unless the user explicitly requests it
- Use `ml-14` on subtitle paragraphs to align with title text
- Include footer with `bg-slate-50` and border-top

**NEVER:**
- Use plain DialogContent without the professional structure
- Skip the cap bar at the top
- Use flat backgrounds in headers
- Use circular icon backgrounds in dialog headers
- Use `bg-white` for main dialog content areas (use `bg-slate-50`)

**Reference examples:**
- `src/components/ActionDropdown.tsx` - Re-assign dialog
- `src/components/news/ArticleEditor.tsx` - Article editor dialog

